    "note": "A frame drum under a muted hand, the slow conversation's other hand (his ear, 10-17): the conga's builder with a wide low head (140 Hz, the conga's 258) that falls only 8 % as the skin lets go, its body under a 650 Hz lowpass, and almost no hand on it (the hand's band at 800 Hz and a twentieth of the conga's level): a thump with a short ring, never a slap. An eight-millisecond attack takes the edge off the landing, and a third of it goes to the room. Rendered alone in a conversation: its energy's mean frequency 140 Hz and none of it over 2 kHz."
